  "query_preview": "..Continuing to see the welcome break for the \npanhandle for this weekend. A building ridge Friday looks to keep \na majority of the precipitation to the west, and with no stronger \nsystem, this ridge does not look to break down easily. Therefore, \nexpect to see a cooling trend going into the weekend, only due to \nsome cloud cover breaking up and radiative cooling dropping most \nof the panhandle below freezing overnight. Not looking to see \nsignificantly below normal temperatures overnight; however, as 850\nmb temperatures still looks significantly above normal for this \ntime of year.\n\nGoing into the work week next week, the marine threat returns.\nWhile there are a variety of different solutions, models have\ngenerally converged that building high pressure in Canada and\nstronger system either moving south or into the south central gulf\nwill generate some stronger northerlies to easterlies out of\nCanada. Could see some precipitation, both rain and snow, but \nlikelihoods at just a chance.",
